@startuml 08-domain-model
skinparam backgroundColor White
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Sans
skinparam roundCorner 6
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam ArrowColor #333333
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFFFF0
skinparam NoteBorderColor #999999
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #F4F4F8
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #555555
skinparam ClassBackgroundColor #F4F4F8
skinparam ClassBorderColor #555555
skinparam StateBackgroundColor #F4F4F8
skinparam StateBorderColor #555555
skinparam ComponentBackgroundColor #F4F4F8
skinparam ComponentBorderColor #555555
title Domain model\nthe value types and what actually gets booked

class Movie <<value>> {
    +MovieId id
    +string title
    +int durationMinutes
    +string language
    +string genre
}

class Theater <<value>> {
    +TheaterId id
    +string name
    +string city
    +int seatCapacity = 20
    +int seatsPerRow = 10
}

class Showtime <<value>> {
    +ShowtimeId id
    +MovieId movieId
    +TheaterId theaterId
    +MinutesSinceMidnight startTime
    +int seatCapacity
    +int seatsPerRow
}

class Booking <<value>> {
    +BookingId id
    +ShowtimeId showtimeId
    +vector<SeatLabel> seats
    +string customerName
    +int64 createdAtEpochSeconds
}

class SeatMap <<behaviour>> {
    -int m_capacity
    -int m_seatsPerRow
    -vector<SeatState> m_seats
    --
    +labelToIndex(label) : optional<size_t>
    +indexToLabel(index) : SeatLabel
    +isFree(label) : bool
    +book(label)
    +release(label)
    +availableSeats() : vector<SeatLabel>
    +relayout(capacity, perRow)
}

enum SeatState {
    Free
    Booked
}

class Catalog <<thread-safe>> {
    -std::mutex m_mutex
    -map<MovieId, Movie> m_movies
    -map<TheaterId, Theater> m_theaters
    -map<ShowtimeId, ShowtimeRecord> m_showtimes
    -map<BookingId, Booking> m_bookings
    --
    +bookSeats(...) : Booking
    +snapshot() : CatalogSnapshot
    +restore(snapshot)
}

class ShowtimeRecord <<internal>> {
    +Showtime showtime
    +SeatMap seats
}

Catalog "1" *-- "many" Movie
Catalog "1" *-- "many" Theater
Catalog "1" *-- "many" ShowtimeRecord
Catalog "1" *-- "many" Booking

ShowtimeRecord *-- "1" Showtime
ShowtimeRecord *-- "1" SeatMap
SeatMap ..> SeatState

Showtime "many" --> "1" Movie : movieId
Showtime "many" --> "1" Theater : theaterId
Booking "many" --> "1" Showtime : showtimeId

note top of Showtime #FFE8E8
  **Showtime is the bookable unit.**
  A Movie is global ("The Silent Protocol" is the
  same film everywhere) and so is a Theater. What
  gets booked is the triple (movie, theater, time),
  and it owns its own seat map - because seat a1 at
  09:00 has nothing to do with seat a1 at 11:00.

  "Which theaters show movie X" is answered by
  scanning showtimes rather than by a stored
  many-to-many table, so there is only one place
  where the truth lives and it cannot go out of sync.
end note

note right of SeatMap #FFF8E0
  Seats are laid out row by row.
  With seatsPerRow = 10:
    index 0..9   -> a1 .. a10
    index 10..19 -> b1 .. b10
  The last row may be partial:
  capacity 12 -> a1..a10, b1, b2.

  Storage is vector<SeatState>, **not**
  vector<bool> - the bool specialisation
  is a proxy container and buys nothing
  at these sizes.
end note

note bottom of Catalog #E8FFE8
  Every getter returns a **copy**. Handing out a
  reference into the maps would let a caller read
  the data after the lock was released - a race
  that compiles perfectly and fails once a month.

  The value types are deliberately dumb (public
  data, no invariants); all invariants live here,
  next to the lock that protects them.
end note

@enduml
